course: dictionary
lesson: 6282
title: Big, shocking or ugly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Monstrous comes from the word monster, but it does not always mean a creature. Use the words around it to decide its meaning. «They were but four in all, but to the panic-stricken weasels the hall seemed full of monstrous animals, grey, black, brown and yellow.» The weasels are terrified, so the animals seem huge and frightening.
explain: Check the clues in the sentence. A monstrous wave is very large and frightening. A monstrous lie is very wrong and shocking. Swap in your meaning, such as «very large and frightening», and see if it still makes sense.
explain: In Alice in Wonderland, Alice grows to a monstrous size. Here the word means very, very big. The sentence tells you what is happening, so you can work out which meaning fits.
explain: Monstrous can also describe something ugly and strange in shape. When you meet a new word, ask yourself what it describes and how the writer feels about it. The clues will tell you which meaning to choose.
fact: Monstrous is an adjective, so it describes a noun, such as a monstrous wave.
fact: Monstrous can mean very large and frightening, like a monster.
fact: Monstrous can mean very wrong, cruel or shocking, as in «a monstrous lie».
fact: Monstrous can also mean ugly and strange in shape.
fact: Monstrous is more monstrous and most monstrous when you compare things.
exercise: «They were but four in all, but to the panic-stricken weasels the hall seemed full of monstrous animals, grey, black, brown and yellow.» What does monstrous mean here? | Very small and harmless | *Very large and frightening | Very quiet and still | Very kind and gentle
exercise: Mum says, «That was a monstrous thing to say to your little brother.» What does monstrous mean here? | Very tidy and neat | Very tall and wide | Very funny and silly | *Very cruel and shocking
exercise: «The weasels were panic-stricken.» What does panic-stricken mean? | Fast and happy | Hungry for food | Very calm and sleepy | *Filled with sudden fear
test: «The sea sent a monstrous wave over the harbour wall.» What does monstrous mean? | Very small and quiet | *Very large and frightening | Very neat and tidy | Very wrong and cruel
test: «The creature had a monstrous, twisted shape.» What does monstrous suggest? | Very tiny and gentle | Very cruel and wicked | *Ugly and strange in shape | Very polite and kind
exam: Which sentence uses monstrous to mean very wrong or shocking? | «The monstrous cake sat on the table.» | «The monstrous hill rose above the valley.» | «The monstrous wave crashed on the rocks.» | *«The mayor called the plan a monstrous betrayal of the town.»
